From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:52:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Trace W^X page flips on macOS.

The two flips in virtual_handle_fault (exec fault: read-write to read-exec;
write fault: read-exec to read-write, see the macOS Apple Silicon W^X patch)
happen on every rewrite-and-run of a JIT page, and nothing showed that they
do or how often. A flip that fails leaves the fault to be raised, which looks
like any other access violation.

Add the debug channel wxflip, off by default. Each flip that succeeds prints
"<page> -> rx" or "<page> -> rw", so WINEDEBUG=+wxflip counts them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index b0607691..750eefe2 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -94,6 +94,9 @@
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(virtual);
 WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(module);
 WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(mem_areas);
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(wxflip);
+#endif
 
 struct preload_info
 {
@@ -4363,7 +4366,10 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_handle_fault( struct thread_data *data, EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec,
             (get_unix_prot( get_page_vprot( addr )) & PROT_WRITE))
         {
             if (!mprotect( page, host_page_size, get_unix_prot( vprot ) & ~PROT_EXEC ))
+            {
+                TRACE_(wxflip)( "%p -> rw\n", page );
                 ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+            }
         }
 #endif
     }
@@ -4373,7 +4379,10 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_handle_fault( struct thread_data *data, EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec,
     {
         /* W^X-degraded host page currently read-write: flip it to read-exec */
         if (!mprotect( page, host_page_size, get_unix_prot( vprot ) & ~PROT_WRITE ))
+        {
+            TRACE_(wxflip)( "%p -> rx\n", page );
             ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+        }
     }
 #endif
     mutex_unlock( &virtual_mutex );
